is it still possible for young people to  flourish in america big questions like  this usually make us think of top-down  answers kids can't get ahead because  capitalism is broken marriage is fail  because the media is setting a bad  example but psychologist yuri  braunfenbrenner's theory of human  development tells a different story he  found that children grow and make  decisions within a layered system of  relationships and that those  relationships with the closest proximity  to a child like families teachers and  strong faith communities have the  greatest influence  other institutions are important but  distant  government media and the larger society  matter less when the core is strong if  we want to truly empower children we  should partner with the people closest  to them  giving parents the power to choose great  schools teaching kids that the family  they form matters or helping young  people recognize the value of a personal  faith commitment  every single effort helps set them up  for future success  to learn more about yuri  bronfenbrenner's theory of human  development check out the links in the  description below also let us know what  other topics you'd like our scholars to  cover in 60 seconds and be sure to like  and subscribe for more research and  videos from aei
 

